@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# Product
+
+This is a compact design-tool entry point, not a second source of intent. The
+authority remains [VISION.md](VISION.md), [UIUX-VISION](docs/specs/ui/UIUX-VISION.md),
+the [UI audit](docs/specs/ui/AUDIT-2026-07-31.md), and
+[ADR-016](docs/adr/ADR-016-cockpit-v2.md). Derived from those existing decisions.
+
+## Register
+
+product
+
+## Users
+
+Geoff operates his local Mac: inspect actual machine state, understand drift,
+review changes, apply with consent, and verify the receipt. New-machine users need
+an understandable path to convergence. Agents consume the same contracts, not a
+private model. Catalog and fleet personas remain subject to their stage gates.
+
+## Product Purpose
+
+One glance should tell the truth about this machine. The cockpit is a projection
+of Conjure's deterministic engine, not a second orchestrator. It is safe to leave
+open for reads; every write follows plan, review, consent, apply, verify, receipt.
+
+## Brand Personality
+
+Calm, precise, accountable. Quiet when clean, explicit when broken. Evidence and a
+useful next action matter more than decoration. Workbench density, not marketing.
+
+## Anti-references
+
+No cloud/IaC console metaphor, ornamental hero sections, invented telemetry, or
+noise that trains the operator to ignore the screen. No success claims from
+unavailable data. No separate GUI runtime or bypass of the consent ceremony.
+
+## Design Principles
+
+- Use canonical engine/domain data; keep provenance and diagnostic evidence near
+  the claim. Missing, stale, failed and empty are different states.
+- Compose app-kit widgets and role tokens; do not fork existing kit components.
+- Organize navigation around the user's model, per ADR-016, not a list of verbs.
+- Preserve last-good dashboard data with a visible age when refresh fails, as
+  specified in SPEC-UI-001 State 5. Never describe it as current.
+- Conjure code stays local until ADR-010's extraction quarantine is satisfied.
+
+## Accessibility & Inclusion
+
+SPEC-UI-001 requires keyboard-reachable controls with visible focus. SPEC-UI-002
+requires safe default focus, managed dialog/drawer focus, escaped evidence and
+polite live progress. Text and status glyphs must convey meaning alongside color.
+Use the existing light/dark/OS theme choice. Keep diagnostics readable on narrow
+screens without hiding their cause. These are requirements, not a claim of a
+completed accessibility audit.
