@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+# Conjure's app-kit adoption
+
+## Current slice and authority
+
+On 2026-09-21 the owner selected Conjure while Fathom has concurrent work. This
+slice repairs dashboard status-read validity under SPEC-UI-001 State 5, not the
+entire cockpit. Preserve canonical engine data, loopback/session authentication,
+the write-consent ceremony, existing dependencies and embedded appearance.
+No real machine state, operational CLI commands, deployment or global configuration.
+
+Baseline: `poc` at `e9d0f2e5d54a3ffd3aca9c548642849e0df274de`, initially clean.
+The source and tests are a working-tree change; no consumer commit/push is part of
+this slice. [PRODUCT.md](../PRODUCT.md) routes design tools to the existing product
+vision; [intent](intent/README.md) and accepted ADRs remain authoritative.
+
+## Use the kit deliberately
+
+Read the applicable UI spec and [component map](specs/ui/COMPONENT-MAP.md), then the
+kit's `docs/design/adoption.md` and `docs/design/contribution-loop.md`. Discover
+first-party capabilities through the `appkit` MCP, inspect their exact source and
+quality evidence, and compose existing APIs before inventing local presentation.
+Tailwind Plus and MatDash are private design references, not proof of a working
+conversion. Never ship an MCP dependency in the running app.
+
+The current Go manifest uses a sibling `replace` and vendored code. That is not an
+immutable app-kit revision pin or a proved clean-clone CSS build. Before any upgrade,
+select an exact kit revision/source closure, review module/token changes, update
+vendor only within approved scope, rebuild scanned CSS and test without the sibling
+checkout. Do not relabel the existing snapshot or copy new packages under old pins.
+No dependency or mirror upgrade was performed in this status-read repair.
+
+## Status-read acceptance
+
+- Failed reads and `(nil, nil)` are unavailable, never empty or converged.
+- Successful empty reads still show the ordinary onboarding hint.
+- Each SSE connection remembers its own last successful status time. Later errors
+  retain its fragments with a visible last-good timestamp; recovery clears the error.
+  This is not a cross-request cache: reconnect/initial-GET continuity is not promised.
+- Complete id-bearing fragments replace their matching elements, never nest a second
+  identical id. Orphan-only status does not claim full convergence.
+- Error text remains escaped, wrapped and announced through a polite status region.
+
+Verification: `go test -race ./internal/webui ./internal/ui -count=1` includes
+`dashboard_validity_test.go` plus `TestDashboardTruthfulStatusStates` and
+`TestDashboardDiagnosticEscapingAndWrapping`. Regenerate only the changed template
+with the manifest-matching tool:
+`go run github.com/a-h/templ/cmd/templ@v0.3.1020 generate -f internal/ui/dashboard.templ`.
+The degraded-banner golden changes only for reviewed announcement/wrapping markup.
+These synthetic Go/HTTP/SSE checks are not browser, screen-reader or human usability
+certification. UI-A plan rows remain unchanged; the full DASH-1 contract is not closed.
+
+## Next bounded tasks and contribution return
+
+1. Independently model failures from Doctor, Runs and SnapshotSize; they still lose
+   error information in `collectDashboardData`. Add fake-source canaries first.
+2. Exercise complete/failure/stale/recovered states in a synthetic browser using the
+   real embedded CSS and Datastar bundle, including repeated-patch id uniqueness,
+   narrow light/dark layouts, keyboard navigation and cancellation.
+3. Review an exact kit/vendor/CSS upgrade before adopting `stat`/`viz` and the
+   SPEC-UI-001 DASH-7 recent-applies sparkline. Do not invent a second metric model.
+
+Return each verified lesson to app-kit with the source identity, reproduction, failed
+and passing evidence, limitations and disposition. This slice returns the missingness
+and SSE patching lesson, not Conjure code: **ADR-010's 90-day solo-managed quarantine
+and named second-consumer requirement still gate extraction.** A shared candidate
+needs kit tests, reviewed API/source closure, consumer revalidation and adoption
+records; never silently fork kit components or claim a local recipe is promoted.
